// Tests for Microsoft style rules on QDoc prose content.
// Each block targets one or more rules; comments indicate expected violations.

// SHOULD WARN: passive voice (Microsoft.Passive)

/*!
    \class QNetworkReply
    \brief Provides a means of accessing network responses.

    The request is sent and a reply is returned by the network manager on \macos {x86_64}.
    Headers are parsed automatically. Errors are reported via the \youtube {dQw4w9WgXcQ} signal on \nullptr failure.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: first-person plural (Microsoft.We)

/*!
    \class QSettings
    \brief Provides persistent application settings.

    We recommend storing all user preferences using this class.
    We've designed the API to be as simple as possible.
    Let's look at how to read a value.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: wordy phrases (Microsoft.Wordiness)

/*!
    \class QTimer
    \brief Provides repetitive and single-shot timers.

    Utilize this class in order to schedule work at a fixed interval on \MACRO1.
    Prior to starting the timer, set the \QtMinorVersion interval in milliseconds.
    A sufficient number of timers can be active at the same time.
    Call stop() as a means to cancel a pending timeout.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: unnecessary adverbs (Microsoft.Adverbs)

/*!
    \fn void QObject::deleteLater()

    Schedules this object for deletion.
    It is very useful when you cannot delete the object directly.
    The object is quickly destroyed after the event loop returns.
    Call this function easily from any thread.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: use contractions (Microsoft.Contractions)

/*!
    \fn bool QFile::open(OpenMode mode)

    Opens the file in the given mode. Returns \c true on success.
    Do not call this function if the file is already open.
    If the path is empty, the function cannot proceed.
    If the file does not exist, it will not be opened.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: Latin abbreviations (Microsoft.Foreign)

/*!
    \fn QVariant QSettings::value(const QString &key) const

    Returns the value for the setting key. The key is case sensitive,
    e.g., "General/fontSize" and "general/fontSize" are different keys.
    The returned value can be of any type, i.e., it depends on what was stored.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: ellipsis in prose (Microsoft.Ellipses)

/*!
    \fn void QIODevice::waitForReadyRead(int msecs)

    Blocks until data is available for reading...
    If msecs is -1, this function will not time out...
*/

// SHOULD WARN: general URL (Microsoft.GeneralURL)

/*!
    \fn void QNetworkRequest::setUrl(const QUrl &url)

    Sets the URL for this network request.
    Pass the URL of the resource you want to access.
    For a general audience, provide the URL as a string.
*/

