/*!
    \class QAbstractItemModel
    \brief We provide the base class for item models.

    This class provides a standard interface for models on \macos and \BUILDVAR that can be used with all of the standard views provided by Qt, including the tree view, the list view, and the table view.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: missing Oxford comma (Microsoft.OxfordComma)

/*!
    \class QSerialPort
    \brief Provides functions for accessing serial ports.

    The class supports reading, writing and seeking within a serial data stream.
    You can configure the baud rate, data bits and parity before opening the port.
    The port supports reading, writing and seeking.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: semicolon in prose (Microsoft.Semicolon)

/*!
    \class QProcess
    \brief Used to start external programs and communicate with them.

    Set the program name; then call start() to launch the process.
    Use write() to send data to the process; use read() to receive output.
*/

